        <review>&lt;p&gt;An astonishing architectural feat of verse. Across &lt;em&gt;Inferno&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Purgatorio&lt;/em&gt;, and &lt;em&gt;Paradiso&lt;/em&gt;, Dante weaves medieval astronomy, Florentine history, and vivid human portraits into a unified hundred-canto journey.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reading with concise endnotes makes the historical references come alive without slowing the momentum of the poetry.&lt;/p&gt;</review>
